"schatze2TitleDay8": "✈️ Farewell to AIDAcosma – Heading Home with Wonderful Memories",

"schaetze2Day1": "On July 4, 2026, the time had finally come: Our adventure on the AIDAcosma began. After three wonderful months on Mallorca, this start felt especially special. This time, we did not have a long journey ahead of us because our temporary home was already on the island. Instead of airport stress, heavy suitcases, and hours of traveling, our plan was simple and relaxed: from Playa de Palma to the harbor and straight onto the ship.\n\nIn the morning, we got into a taxi with our suitcases and made our way to the cruise terminal in Palma. The ride took about half an hour. For anyone who might want to travel from Playa de Palma to the port themselves: A taxi ride normally costs around 40 euros. A little tip from our own experience: You should always keep an eye on the price when taking taxis, because sometimes a few extra euros are added, which can make the ride noticeably more expensive in the end.\n\nWhen we arrived at the port, that special cruise feeling immediately came over us. Right in front of us was the AIDAcosma – our home for the next few days. And the best part: Because we had booked early check-in, we were allowed to board very early. At around 7:45 a.m., we were already stepping onto the ship.\n\nIt was incredibly pleasant because everything was still calm and relaxed. The check-in went super quickly, there were hardly any people around yet, and we were able to truly enjoy our first moments on board. That feeling when you step onto the ship and realize: Now the journey is really beginning – that is always something very special.\n\nSince our cabin was not ready yet, we started the day exactly the way we love it: with a cozy breakfast at the Steakhouse. The Steakhouse on the AIDAcosma is simply one of our favorite places on board. We especially love that you can also sit outside on the outdoor deck. With a view of the sea, fresh air, and that special holiday feeling, a first day of travel could hardly begin any better.\n\nWhile we were having breakfast, we even had a beautiful view of Palma. From the Steakhouse, we could see the impressive cathedral among other things. That moment, with a delicious breakfast in front of us and the view of Mallorca, was simply perfect.\n\nWe really took our time during breakfast and enjoyed every moment. My mom especially loves the minute steak for breakfast, while I always look forward to the delicious pancakes with fruit salad. Add a fresh fruit plate and a cold cocoa – that is exactly how a perfect holiday day begins for us.\n\nWe stayed at breakfast for a long time and simply enjoyed the moment. No stress, no rush – just arriving, enjoying ourselves, and looking forward to a new journey beginning.\n\nAround 11 a.m., our cabin was finally ready. We were able to move into our home for the next few days, and shortly afterwards our suitcases arrived as well. It was incredibly convenient and relaxing. We immediately started unpacking, organizing everything in the closets, and settling in. Especially on a one-week cruise, it is absolutely worth unpacking everything right away and truly arriving.\n\nOf course, our first little moment of enjoyment could not be missing afterwards: our first milkshake of the trip. We absolutely love the milkshakes on board the AIDAcosma. So our first stop was one of the bars to enjoy this little holiday moment. A cold, delicious milkshake in our hands, exploring the ship, and knowing: The next few days belong only to us – that is exactly why we love cruises.\n\nAt 3 p.m., the next highlight followed: coffee and cake. On AIDA, this little tradition is simply part of the experience. I got myself a slice of strawberry cheesecake, and we started the afternoon in a very relaxed way.\n\nAfter that, we went to the spa. We had booked the Comfort All-In package, which includes, among other things, two hours of spa time per day. Especially on the first day, this was absolutely wonderful. The ship was still pleasantly quiet, many guests had not fully arrived yet, and we were able to enjoy the peaceful atmosphere. We relaxed in the whirlpool, let the day sink in, and simply enjoyed the feeling of having just started our journey.\n\nAfterwards, the safety drill was on the schedule. Then it was already time for dinner. At 6 p.m., we went back to the Steakhouse – one of our favorite places on the AIDAcosma.\n\nWe have eaten at the Steakhouse many times before and simply love the cozy atmosphere there. This time, however, the menu was slightly different, which was a little disappointing because we missed some of our familiar favorite dishes. Nevertheless, the food was delicious again. We were especially impressed by the sweet potato rolls, which were absolutely amazing. The shrimp in garlic oil were also a real highlight.\n\nFor the main course, there was of course steak again – my mom had a delicious steak that she really enjoyed. It was once again that typical AIDA moment: great food, a beautiful atmosphere, and the feeling of truly having arrived on vacation.\n\nIn the evening, we watched the Prime Time together at 8 p.m. and then looked forward to the highlight of the day: the departure. At around 10 p.m., the moment finally arrived. The AIDAcosma slowly started moving, and we sailed out of the port of Palma. The moment when we passed the cathedral was especially beautiful. The city lights, the sea, the ship beneath us, and the feeling that our journey was truly beginning – simply unforgettable.\n\nOur first day on the AIDAcosma could hardly have been more perfect. From the relaxed taxi ride, the early check-in, the breakfast with a sea view, the first milkshakes, wellness, delicious food, all the way to the departure in the evening – everything was included that we love about cruising.\n\nEspecially the early check-in was a really great decision. It allowed us to experience the ship during its quiet phase, arrive without stress, and truly enjoy the first day.\n\nWith the view of the sea and the AIDAcosma slowly leaving Mallorca behind, we knew: The next few days were going to be something very special. 🌊✨",

"schaetze2Day2": "After our exciting first day on board the AIDAcosma, our second day started in a wonderfully relaxed way: a classic sea day. No alarm clock, no excursion, no time pressure – simply enjoying the sea and letting the moment on the ship sink in.\n\nSince we had a Veranda Comfort cabin, our morning already started with a little highlight: We woke up to a beautiful view of the sea. That feeling of opening the curtains and seeing the endless ocean right in front of you is simply something special. These are exactly the moments why we love cruises.\n\nWe actually slept through breakfast that morning – but that was absolutely no problem. Especially on sea days, we like to take things a little slower and enjoy a relaxed start to the day. So we got ready comfortably and first went to the bar to get something to drink.\n\nThere, we immediately discovered a little highlight in the Theatrium: The AIDA Clubby Parade was currently making its way through the ship. Especially for children, this is of course a wonderful experience. The music, the atmosphere, and the bright eyes of the younger guests make moments like these on board truly special.\n\nAfterwards, we walked around the onboard shops a little and took a closer look at the new AIDA Clubbies. We have to honestly say: Our personal favorites are still the old Clubbies. We simply found them prettier and somehow more familiar. Of course, we understand that AIDA wants to change and renew some things after 30 years, but we would have preferred if the old characters had simply been modernized instead of being completely redesigned. But tastes are different, as everyone knows.\n\nBy then it was already lunchtime, and since we had skipped breakfast, we were naturally hungry. So we went for lunch. Afterwards, the day became a little quieter: I used the afternoon to study while we could still enjoy that special atmosphere on board.\n\nIn the afternoon, we treated ourselves to something delicious: brownies from the Street Food area of the AIDAcosma. These little moments of enjoyment are simply part of a cruise for us. Just getting something sweet in between, sitting somewhere, and enjoying the view of the sea – that is what vacation is all about.\n\nAfterwards, we explored the ship a little more and enjoyed the view. We also visited the so-called Skywalk area of the AIDAcosma. However, it has to be said that this area is not quite comparable to the beautiful Skywalks on the AIDAperla or AIDAprima with the glass elevator and impressive construction. On the AIDAcosma, it is more of a viewing platform. Nevertheless, the view of the sea was absolutely beautiful, and we simply enjoyed the moment.\n\nIn the evening, we went to dinner at Mama Mia – one of the specialty restaurants on board. What is especially nice is that the restaurant is already included in the cruise fare and you can eat there without an additional charge. And the food was really delicious.\n\nOur personal highlight was the parmesan soup – we can truly recommend it. It was incredibly creamy and the taste was simply perfect. Afterwards, we had pasta with shrimp, which was also really delicious.\n\nAfter dinner, we made ourselves comfortable and, as every evening, first watched the AIDA Prime Time with Tom. This is simply part of a cruise for us and is always a lovely way to end the day, seeing what happened on board and what highlights are coming next.\n\nTo finish this relaxing sea day, we enjoyed the sunset from our veranda. With the view of the sea, the peaceful surroundings, and the feeling of being exactly where we wanted to be, another beautiful day aboard the AIDAcosma came to an end.\n\nA sea day does not need to be full of activities – sometimes it is exactly these quiet moments that make a journey special. Sleeping in, watching the sea, enjoying good food, and spending time together. That is exactly why we love cruises. 🌅",

"schaetze2Day3": "After a relaxing sea day, the first port stop of our journey finally awaited us on the third day: Cagliari in Sardinia. It was our first time visiting this place – and our anticipation was therefore especially high. We had often heard that Cagliari was supposed to be incredibly beautiful, and we were excited to discover the city for ourselves.\n\nOur day started relatively early because, for us, arriving in a new port is simply one of the most beautiful moments of a cruise. So we made ourselves comfortable on our veranda and watched as the AIDAcosma slowly entered the port of Cagliari. Luckily, our cabin was on the harbor side, which meant we had the perfect view of the entire moment.\n\nThe arrival was truly beautiful. Watching the ship slowly get closer to the coastline, seeing the city grow larger, and watching the landscape open up in front of us is always a very special feeling. These are exactly the moments we enjoy most from our balcony – just like the departure in the evening. There is simply nothing better than experiencing these special moments from your own cabin with a view of the sea.\n\nAfter enjoying the view from our balcony, we went to the Steakhouse for breakfast. Once again, it was incredibly delicious. We simply love having breakfast there in peace, enjoying the sea view, and starting a new vacation day in a relaxed way.\n\nAfterwards, we got ready to explore Cagliari. Since it was our first visit to the city, we naturally wanted to see as much as possible. When we left the ship, we immediately spotted a little tourist train and spontaneously decided to discover the city this way.\n\nThe ride cost 15 euros per person and lasted about one hour. The route took us through different parts of the city, past the old town, through small streets, to beautiful viewpoints, and even to the old prison. It was a really pleasant way to get a first impression of Cagliari and simply let the city unfold around us in a relaxed way.\n\nAlternatively, it would have been possible to book a transfer to the beach. This cost around 12 euros per person for a round trip and was used by many guests. Some fellow travelers also chose a hop-on-hop-off bus tour. However, we were very happy with our decision to take the little train – especially for a first visit, it was a wonderful way to collect many different impressions.\n\nAt the end of the ride, there was the option to either get off again at the port or stay in the city. An important thing to know: If you get off in the city, you cannot later take the little train back to the port. However, walking back is not a problem at all, as it only takes around five minutes from the city center to the harbor.\n\nWe decided to get off in the city and explore Cagliari a little more on foot. We especially loved the small streets, the old buildings, and the Mediterranean atmosphere. Simply walking through the streets without any time pressure, discovering new corners, and enjoying the feeling of the city – those are exactly the moments that make a vacation day special.\n\nAfterwards, we made our way back to the ship. Since we left relatively early, there was not much time left to enjoy the almost empty ship. Nevertheless, we took advantage of the peaceful atmosphere for a little while longer and then went to the spa area. After a beautiful day exploring, it was exactly what we needed: relaxing a bit and enjoying the calm atmosphere on board.\n\nThen came the next special moment: sailing away from Cagliari. Of course, we watched this moment from our cabin again. The ship slowly left the harbor, the coastline became smaller, and once again the endless sea stretched out in front of us – a feeling we love on every cruise.\n\nIn the evening, we went back to the Steakhouse for dinner. There, we ended the day in a cozy atmosphere and once again enjoyed the delicious food and wonderful surroundings.\n\nAfter dinner, we made a little stop at the AIDA Shopping World. Of course, a magnet as a memory of our trip could not be missing. These little souvenirs are simply part of our travels and always remind us of the special moments of a journey later on.\n\nTo finish the day, we watched the AIDA Prime Time and then sat comfortably on our balcony. We listened to the sound of the waves, looked out over the endless sea, and simply enjoyed this moment.\n\nAnother beautiful day aboard the AIDAcosma came to an end – filled with new impressions, Mediterranean memories, and that very special cruise feeling that is difficult to describe. 🌊",

"schaetze2Day4": "After the first exciting days of our journey, today was a little different: Civitavecchia. For many guests, this port is the starting point for an excursion to Rome – a city that we truly love. However, this time we consciously decided to stay on board the AIDAcosma and enjoy the day in a different way.\n\nCivitavecchia and Rome are not new destinations for us. We have already been to Civitavecchia four times, and we have also visited Rome several times. Especially for such a short stay during a cruise day, Rome is simply not the same for us. This beautiful city deserves much more time – with relaxed walks through the small streets, delicious food in an Italian restaurant, and the feeling of really taking in the atmosphere. If we return to Rome, we would rather stay for a few days to truly enjoy everything this special city has to offer.\n\nSo we decided to spend this day on the AIDAcosma and enjoy the almost empty ship. It is always such a special feeling when many guests are away on excursions and you suddenly experience the ship in a completely different way. It is quieter, more relaxed, and you discover places that you sometimes do not have enough time for during a normal day on board.\n\nFor me, today was mainly about studying. While the AIDAcosma was sailing through the Mediterranean, I found a quiet place and used the day to catch up on some things. Even though studying during a vacation might not sound relaxing at first, doing it with a sea view and the special atmosphere on board felt completely different.\n\nOf course, a little break was needed in between. And what is something that simply belongs on an AIDA cruise? Exactly – currywurst. So I went to the currywurst stand on board. The currywurst on AIDA is always a little highlight for us and simply incredibly delicious. It is exactly these small things that make a cruise so special: taking a short break, eating something tasty, and having the feeling of being right in the middle of the ocean.\n\nIn the evening, another special culinary experience was waiting for us: We went to the Sushi House and had Hot Pot. It was really delicious and a wonderful change from our previous restaurant visits. Sitting together while eating, looking back on the day, and simply enjoying our time on board – that is exactly why we love cruises.\n\nAfter dinner, another special moment could not be missed: the departure. Even though we already knew the port of Civitavecchia, every departure is fascinating all over again. The ship slowly starts moving, the lights of the harbor become smaller, and once again there is nothing but the endless sea ahead of us.\n\nWe consciously enjoyed this moment again and let the view from our cabin sink in. The sound of the waves, the fresh air, and the feeling that the next adventure is already waiting – these are exactly the moments that make cruising so special for us.\n\nDay 4 might not have been a classic sightseeing day, but these quiet days are just as much a part of a perfect journey for us. Sometimes it is not the big attractions, but the small moments on board that stay in your memory. 🌊✨",

"schaetze2Day5": "After a relaxing day on board during our stop in Civitavecchia, today we were looking forward to a destination we were especially excited about: Ajaccio on Corsica.\n\nWe already knew Ajaccio from our trip last year – and that was exactly why we were so excited to return. Last year, this city immediately impressed us with its special charm, Mediterranean atmosphere, and its beautiful location right by the sea. There are places where you are simply happy to come back again – and Ajaccio is definitely one of those places for us.\n\nOur day started once again with a very special cruise moment: arriving in port. Since we only arrived later in the harbor, we could comfortably watch from our veranda as the AIDAcosma slowly approached the coast of Corsica.\n\nAnd this arrival was truly spectacular. While the ship was slowly heading towards the harbor, we were suddenly surprised by a small air show. Two glider planes flew over the water and put on a really impressive performance. They flew sideways through the air at times, performed spectacular movements, and repeatedly came very close to the surface of the water. The most impressive moment was when they flew so low over the sea that they almost touched the water before pulling back up and disappearing over the mountains.\n\nThese unexpected moments are what make a cruise so special. You are simply sitting on your balcony, enjoying the view – and suddenly something happens that you never expected.\n\nAfter enjoying the arrival, we first went to the Steakhouse for breakfast. Once again, it was absolutely delicious. We simply love starting the day in a relaxed way with a good breakfast and a view of the sea.\n\nAfter that, we made our way off the ship. The great thing about Ajaccio is that the cruise ship arrives directly in the city. The port is located right in the city center, so there are no long walks or transfers needed. Within just a few minutes, you are right in the middle of the city and can start exploring immediately.\n\nOur first stop was the market in Ajaccio. We are noticing more and more that we really enjoy visiting markets. There is simply something special about walking between the different stalls, discovering local products, and taking in the atmosphere.\n\nWe looked around at a relaxed pace and also remembered our visit from last year. Unfortunately, some of the stalls we had seen back then were no longer there this time. We were especially sad that a stall selling fried little balls had disappeared. We discovered these little treats last year and were absolutely amazed by them. There were different varieties, including ones filled with Nutella, cheese, or savory versions. They were incredibly delicious, and we had actually been looking forward to eating them again.\n\nUnfortunately, the older lady who had run the stall back then was no longer there this time. We assume that she may have retired by now. Of course, it is a little sad, but these kinds of changes are simply part of traveling. Some things remain beautiful memories from past journeys.\n\nAfter visiting the market, we continued on to the Galeari pastry shop. It is located directly behind the market, just a short walk uphill, and can be reached within a few minutes from the cruise port. They have incredibly delicious strawberry pastries – and we can honestly say: They were fantastic. A small sweet moment of indulgence in the middle of Ajaccio that we really enjoyed.\n\nAfterwards, we simply wandered through the city at a relaxed pace. Without a big plan, just letting ourselves be guided by the moment. We passed several churches, explored the small streets, and enjoyed the French-Mediterranean atmosphere.\n\nAlong the way, we also passed the Napoleon Library, the Bibliothèque Fesch, which is named after Cardinal Joseph Fesch and houses an impressive collection. We also walked past Maison Bonaparte, the birthplace of Napoleon Bonaparte. However, this time we did not visit it and only looked at it from the outside.\n\nOur tip: If you would like to visit Maison Bonaparte, you should definitely go very early – ideally right after arriving in port. Later in the day, long lines can form and you can quickly lose a lot of time.\n\nAfter our walk, we returned to the AIDAcosma. There, we enjoyed the quiet atmosphere on board and relaxed in the whirlpool. After a beautiful day on land, it was exactly what we needed: coming back to the ship, switching off, and continuing to enjoy our vacation moment.\n\nOf course, the departure in the evening could not be missed. Once again, we made ourselves comfortable on our veranda and watched as the AIDAcosma slowly left Ajaccio behind. These moments from our balcony are simply some of our favorite experiences on a cruise.\n\nIn the evening, we had another lovely activity planned. We watched the show \"Pyramide\" in Studio X, which was really entertaining. Afterwards, we went to the Steakhouse for dinner, where we ended the day with delicious food in a cozy atmosphere.\n\nAfterwards, we watched the AIDA Prime Time and relaxed for the rest of the evening. To finish the day, we sat outside on our balcony again, watched the sunset, and simply enjoyed the peacefulness of the sea.\n\nDay 5 was exactly how we imagine a perfect cruise day: a beautiful port, special moments while arriving, delicious food, little discoveries in the city, and finally the peace and quiet of our own balcony.\n\nAjaccio enchanted us once again on our second visit – and we are sure this place will stay in our memories for a very long time. ✨",
"schaetze2Day6": "After our wonderful day in Ajaccio, Marseille was on our itinerary today. For many cruise passengers, Marseille is a popular starting point for excursions to Provence or for exploring the city itself. For us, however, it was not a destination we were particularly excited about. Nevertheless, we wanted to take a quick look at the city and at least explore the harbor area.\n\nWe took the morning very slowly and went off the ship a little later. Our original plan was to use the free shuttle bus provided by Marseille. The AIDA shuttle directly into the city costs 19 euros per person, so of course we first looked for the free alternative.\n\nHowever, the free shuttle does not leave directly from the ship. When you leave the ship, you have to walk to the left and after about five minutes you reach the shuttle departure area. In general, this is a great way to get into the city for free – but there is one small catch.\n\nWhile AIDA operates shuttle buses regularly, Marseille’s free shuttle only has one single bus. It arrives approximately every 35 minutes. When we arrived there, the queue was already incredibly long. After a quick estimate, we probably would have had to wait at least one and a half hours before we could even get on the bus.\n\nAnd honestly: It just was not worth it for us. Especially on a cruise, you want to enjoy the day and not spend a large part of it standing in a queue. So we spontaneously decided to turn around and go back on board.\n\nOur tip for anyone visiting Marseille: If you want to use the free shuttle, make sure to leave the ship immediately after arrival and try to catch the first bus. That way, you have a much better chance of getting into the city without a long wait. Alternatively, a taxi can also be a good option – the ride takes around 16 minutes. Or you can use the AIDA shuttle for 19 euros per person if you prefer the easiest option.\n\nSince Marseille is not one of our favorite destinations anyway and we only wanted to take a quick look at the city, it honestly was not a problem for us in the end. We decided to use the day differently – and that is exactly what is so great about cruising: You do not always have to leave the ship. Sometimes the most beautiful moments are the quiet days on board.\n\nBack on the AIDAcosma, we enjoyed the almost empty ship. It was incredibly relaxing because many guests were out exploring. We were able to fully enjoy the peaceful atmosphere on board, switch off for a while, and simply enjoy the moment.\n\nOf course, a visit to the spa was also a must. Days like this are perfect for simply doing nothing, relaxing in the whirlpool, and enjoying the view of the sea.\n\nAt lunchtime, we went to the Brauhaus for a meal. The food there was once again really delicious and was perfect for our relaxing day on board. It is exactly these little moments of enjoyment that make cruising so special for us: good food, a sea view, and simply spending time together.\n\nIn the afternoon, we continued to take things slowly and enjoyed some more free time on the ship.\n\nIn the evening, one of our favorite moments came again: departure. We made ourselves comfortable on our veranda and watched as the AIDAcosma left Marseille behind and headed towards the next adventure.\n\nEven though Marseille was not a classic highlight port for us on this trip, it was still a beautiful day. Because sometimes a vacation does not mean filling every moment with activities. Sometimes it simply means having the ship almost to yourself, relaxing, and enjoying the moment.\n\nAnd that is exactly what we did today. 🌊✨",

"schaetze2Day7": "After a week full of wonderful moments on board the AIDAcosma, one very special highlight was waiting for us today: Barcelona. We were really looking forward to this port because Barcelona is definitely one of our favorite cities. We love the combination of the old city with its small streets, impressive buildings, many shops, and at the same time the modern atmosphere.\n\nWe started the morning in a relaxed way and got ready to leave the AIDAcosma for our last big shore excursion of this trip.\n\nThere are several options for getting from the port into the city. AIDA offers its own shuttle bus, which costs 12 euros per person. However, there is also a shuttle provided by Barcelona itself, which only costs 4.50 euros per person. Of course, we chose the cheaper option – and the best part is: both shuttles drop you off at the same place in the city. For us, it simply does not make sense to spend more money when you arrive at exactly the same destination.\n\nOur very first stop after arriving was a place that we absolutely love in Barcelona: the Mercat de Sant Josep de la Boqueria, better known as Mercat La Boqueria. This famous market in the middle of La Rambla is always an experience. The many colors, smells, and stalls filled with fresh products immediately make you feel like you are right in the middle of Spanish life.\n\nOf course, we couldn’t just walk through without trying something. Our first stop was the freshly made smoothies. I chose strawberry-banana and my mom chose mango-passion fruit. Both were incredibly delicious and exactly what we needed on a warm day in Barcelona.\n\nAfter that, we discovered even more delicious things. We bought fresh salami sticks and different types of salami, including ones with a pepper coating. The quality and taste were simply fantastic. Of course, something sweet couldn’t be missing either: I treated myself to fresh strawberries with Nutella – a little indulgent moment that you just have to allow yourself on vacation.\n\nAfter exploring the market in detail, we continued through the city. And as always happens in Barcelona: we went shopping. Barcelona is simply perfect for that – and every time we promise ourselves not to buy too much. But somehow it never works out. In the end, we always end up carrying far too many shopping bags.\n\nWhat makes Barcelona so special for us is this mixture of different worlds. The city is incredibly spacious and combines the historic old town with modern neighborhoods. We love exactly this variety.\n\nOur walk first took us toward the cathedral and through the beautiful little streets of the old town. We strolled through the narrow streets, admired the impressive buildings, and simply enjoyed the atmosphere.\n\nAfter that, we continued into the more modern part of the city. Barcelona simply invites you to walk around without a fixed plan and discover new corners again and again.\n\nOn our way back to our favorite restaurant, we made a special stop: the Sephora with the famous slide. Yes, you read that correctly – you can actually slide through the store there. Of course, we had to try it. It was such a fun moment and definitely something you do not experience every day.\n\nOf course, a little shopping stop could not be missing either: we bought new Stanley cups, which will now always remind us of this trip.\n\nWe also stopped by the famous McDonald’s with the mosaic design. We had heard a lot about it and wanted to see it for ourselves. However, we have to be honest: for us, the extra walk was not really worth it. It was interesting to see, but we would not go out of our way to visit it again.\n\nThen came the culinary highlight of our Barcelona day: our favorite restaurant, El Pintxo de Petritxol. This restaurant is located right near the cathedral and is simply part of every Barcelona visit for us.\n\nThey serve incredibly delicious pintxos and tapas, as well as other Spanish specialties such as paella. We especially love the tapas – every single dish is full of flavor, and you can really taste the attention to detail.\n\nFor us, it is always a special moment to sit there, eat together, and know: We have been here before, and that is exactly why we always come back.\n\nAfter this beautiful day, we returned to the AIDAcosma. When we left the cabin in the morning, we had already left a tip for our cabin attendant. She was incredibly kind and attentive throughout the trip, and we always like to give something back at the end of a journey.\n\nWhen we returned to our cabin after our Barcelona excursion, we were greeted by a wonderful surprise: beautiful hearts had been created on our bed using the towels and the blanket. Small gestures like this really make a difference. You can see how much effort the crew puts into making guests’ time on board special.\n\nIn the evening, one last big cruise moment was waiting for us: sailing away from Barcelona. At 6 p.m., we made ourselves comfortable on our veranda and watched as the AIDAcosma slowly left the harbor.\n\nWhile we were sailing away, another cruise ship passed by us: the Aroya. It was a beautiful sight to see both ships on the water.\n\nAfter leaving the port, we went to the Steakhouse one more time for dinner. One last time, we enjoyed our favorite restaurant on board, looked back on the journey, and enjoyed this very special final evening.\n\nAfter that, unfortunately, it was already time to pack our suitcases. The last things were put away, and we realized that our beautiful journey was slowly coming to an end.\n\nBarcelona was the perfect ending to this cruise. A city full of life, enjoyment, memories, and special moments. And it is exactly this combination of amazing ports and relaxing moments on board that makes our AIDAcosma journeys so unique for us. 🌊✨",
"schaetze2Day8": "How quickly time passes… Today was unfortunately already the final day of our wonderful journey with the AIDAcosma. After many special moments, amazing ports, delicious food, and countless memories, it was time to say goodbye.\n\nThe last morning on board was very relaxed. We went for breakfast one more time and enjoyed the atmosphere on the ship for the final time. This is a feeling that probably every cruise lover knows: You sit there, look around one last time, and think about how quickly the past days have flown by.\n\nAfter breakfast, we collected our belongings, got ready for departure, and had to leave our cabin with a heavy heart. One week on the AIDAcosma had come to an end.\n\nThen came the moment that everyone would probably like to avoid on a cruise: leaving the ship for the last time. We said goodbye to the AIDAcosma and made our way back to Playa de Palma.\n\nSince we wanted to spend one more night on Mallorca, we returned to the hotel. This allowed us to end the trip in a relaxed way and meant we did not have to continue traveling immediately after the cruise.\n\nThe next day, our next little adventure was already waiting for us: we took the ferry from Mallorca to Barcelona and then continued home by car.\n\nWith that, our cruise adventure with the AIDAcosma officially came to an end. A journey full of beautiful memories: from the relaxed arrival, to the special moments on board, the breathtaking sunsets on our veranda, delicious meals in our favorite restaurants, beautiful cities like Cagliari, Ajaccio, and Barcelona, all the way to the peaceful moments at sea.\n\nOnce again, this cruise showed us why we love traveling with AIDA so much. It is this special combination of exploring, relaxing, enjoying, and simply spending time together that makes these journeys so special.\n\nWith many new memories in our luggage, we headed home – but of course not without thinking: The next trip is sure to come. 🌊❤️"
  }